{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400840-animal-latent-abilities","id":1400840,"title":"Animal Latent Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-03T16:01:21-07:00","id":1400840,"title":"Animal Latent Abilities","content":"So, I\u2019m playing in a game at the moment where I\u2019m a lunar who was concentrating on having multitudes of animal forms and swift shifting to be some kind of animal shaman dude. <br /> <br /> Anyway; I was looking to buy some Latent abilities to share between forms and our group got into a debate as to wether this should be allowed. <br /> <br /> Based on the text on pg. 555 of the core; my GM has determined that animals should be able to learn \u201cany merit or special attack\u201d from any other animal as a latent ability- provided the animal has the capacity to use it (like dive attacks only for animals with wings, grapple abilities only for animals that \u2018depend on grapples\u2019 and such as per a lot of the text in those abilities) - but my group is still torn on what looks to be an unbalancing conglomerate of free abilities (at 6exp a pop).<br /> <br /> As the player asking for this, I don\u2019t feel qualified to make a list of abilities I feel are mechanically okay - so to help out my GM, are there any animal abilities people would feel should just be totally struck off the list as too unbalancing to be shared with other animal forms?<br /> <br /> Any help Much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T18:06:18-07:00","id":1400867,"title":"","content":"My read of pg 555 is that only the latent abilities on pg 555 are more or less generic, and other abilities are by default not learnable and can be if there's an argument for it.<br /> <br /> As for things under no circumstance learnable: Legendary Size, Tiny Size, Minuscule Size<br /> I would generally be extremely wary of anything that adds dice to a combat action. Or damage to an attack. Or of adding anything possessed by a legendary size creature to a non-legendary size creature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T18:55:29-07:00","id":1400876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400840-animal-latent-abilities?p=1400867#post1400867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would generally be extremely wary of anything that adds dice to a combat action. Or damage to an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>A benthic knifetooth learning to use a snake's crushing constriction attack with its neck is given as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T19:51:10-07:00","id":1400883,"title":"","content":"Any of the unique Tyrant Lizard attacks and merits should be of the table for sure, they're bad enough with Tyrant Lizards themselves. Really any unique combat merits like Underfoot Menace, Blade-Beak Frenzy, or Death Roll are likely to be a problem and the generic merits like Deadly Charge, Gore, Trample, etc. are probably safer.<br /> <br /> Other than that I would be more carefull about what animal forms you allow the latent abilities to work for more than what abilities can be learned. F.ex. hippos, pestletails, cats, and the legendary size dinosaurs are all incredibly strong already and giving them access to even more merits is kinda overkill. OTOH letting some extra merits that seem appropriate be accessed in bear, wolf, or great-cat forms isn't likely to break anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:14:39-07:00","id":1400886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400840-animal-latent-abilities?p=1400876#post1400876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A benthic knifetooth learning to use a snake's crushing constriction attack with its neck is given as an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bad example, since constriction in snakes isn't just brute force choking. It's targeted toward altering the blood pressure and stopping the heart directly, which frilled sharks probably can't do, as their bodies are honed for swimming instead of ambush hunting and abdominally massaging prospective food items to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T03:11:54-07:00","id":1401883,"title":"","content":"I mean a lot of it can probably decided at the table on a case-by-case basis.<br /> Underfoot menace can probably be taught to a racoon, because it's about a cat's size and has claws, maybe even a snake, because it might scurry around someone's feet, and can bite, but not something too large for that, like a wolf.<br /> You can probably teach a non-bird to go for someone's eyes, but certainly not to dive-attack.<br /> Your mileage may vary depending on how many zoologists are at your table, because while Saur Ops Specialist is obviously right, from a purely cinematic perspective I don't see anything wrong with a benthic knifetooth, or a moray eel, snake-choking someone. Even though they use their musculature for swimming and probably lack the anatomy to actually grapple with their entire body.<br /> <br /> Edit: in the end I feel like cheesing latent abilities a bit &quot;only&quot; means that you get into the territories of Solar melee or brawl with stacking bonuses, which is ridiculously strong, but you are playing a Celestial Exalt, so why the hell not. Sure it gets really strong, but you can also just havel like 50 soak as a Lunar, so might as well be the deadliest opossum to ever strangulate someone with it's tail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T20:49:37-07:00","id":1402182,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your thoughts. I\u2019ll run some stuff by my GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}